---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const featured = (await getCollection('use-cases'))
  .filter((c) => c.data.featured)
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
---

<Layout
  title="Creative AI Explorer"
  description="Explore current and emerging creative AI tools, workflows, and future trajectories across image, video, music, writing, and agentic systems. Updated for 2026."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <Hero />

    <!-- Current Landscape -->
    <section id="current" class="section-padding border-t border-slate-800/60">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <div class="mb-12 max-w-2xl">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-400 mb-3">Now</p>
          <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">The 2026 Creative AI Landscape</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            Creative practice has moved past early novelty. The dominant pattern is hybrid human–AI workflows
            where models handle volume, variation, and continuity while humans retain direction, taste, and final accountability.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <article class="card">
            <div class="mb-4 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-brand-500/15 text-brand-400">
              <svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M4 16l4.586-4.586a2 2 0 012.828 0L16 16m-2-2l1.586-1.586a2 2 0 012.828 0L20 14m-6-6h.01M6 20h12a2 2 0 002-2V6a2 2 0 00-2-2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z" /></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Visual Generation</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
              High-fidelity image models with strong prompt adherence, style control, and reference-driven consistency.
              Inpainting, control nets, and upscalers form the everyday toolkit for concept art, product visualization, and marketing assets.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <div class="mb-4 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-accent-500/15 text-accent-400">
              <svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M15 10l4.553-2.276A1 1 0 0121 8.618v6.764a1 1 0 01-1.447.894L15 14M5 18h8a2 2 0 002-2V8a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z" /></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Video & Motion</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
              Runway, Kling, Luma and related systems now support longer coherent clips, better character persistence,
              and usable camera language. Short-form narrative and product motion are increasingly viable for small teams.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <div class="mb-4 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/15 text-emerald-400">
              <svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M9 19V6l12-3v13M9 19c0 1.105-1.343 2-3 2s-3-.895-3-2 1.343-2 3-2 3 .895 3 2zm12-3c0 1.105-1.343 2-3 2s-3-.895-3-2 1.343-2 3-2 3 .895 3 2zM9 10l12-3" /></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Music & Audio</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
              Suno, Udio and specialized models accelerate sketching, arrangement, and stem generation.
              Hybrid DAW workflows remain standard for professional release quality and emotional nuance.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <div class="mb-4 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-amber-500/15 text-amber-400">
              <svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M11 5H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v11a2 2 0 002 2h11a2 2 0 002-2v-5m-1.414-9.414a2 2 0 112.828 2.828L11.828 15H9v-2.828l8.586-8.586z" /></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Writing & Narrative</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
              Large language models serve as ideation partners, structural editors, and world-building assistants.
              Human judgment remains decisive for voice, originality, and final authorship decisions.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <div class="mb-4 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-rose-500/15 text-rose-400">
              <svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M9.75 17L9 20l-1 1h8l-1-1-.75-3M3 13h18M5 17h14a2 2 0 002-2V5a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z" /></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Agentic Systems</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
              Multi-step agents that plan, generate, critique, and revise are moving from research demos into
              production creative stacks. Direction is shifting from tool switching to high-level intent.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <div class="mb-4 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-sky-500/15 text-sky-400">
              <svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" /></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Consistency & Control</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
              Character sheets, visual bibles, reference locking, and style systems have made multi-scene
              and multi-episode AI-assisted production practical for independent creators.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Featured Use Cases -->
    <section id="use-cases" class="section-padding border-t border-slate-800/60 bg-slate-900/30">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <div class="mb-12 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-end sm:justify-between gap-4">
          <div class="max-w-xl">
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-400 mb-3">Practice</p>
            <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Featured Use Cases</h2>
            <p class="text-slate-400">Concrete patterns creators and teams are applying right now.</p>
          </div>
          <a href="/explorations" class="btn-secondary text-sm shrink-0">
            All explorations →
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
          {featured.map((item) => (
            <a href={`/explorations/${item.slug}`} class="card group block">
              <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-400 mb-2">
                {item.data.category}
              </p>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white group-hover:text-brand-300 transition mb-2">
                {item.data.title}
              </h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                {item.data.description}
              </p>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Future -->
    <section id="future" class="section-padding border-t border-slate-800/60">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <div class="mb-12 max-w-2xl">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-400 mb-3">Trajectory</p>
          <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Where Creative AI Is Heading</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            The next phase is less about single spectacular generations and more about reliable, controllable,
            multi-step creative systems that amplify human intent at scale.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="card flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6">
            <div class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-brand-500/15 text-brand-400 text-lg font-bold">
              01
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">From Tools to Directed Systems</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
                Creators will increasingly set high-level creative goals and constraints; agentic layers will
                orchestrate the model chain, surface decision points, and maintain continuity across long-form or multi-asset projects.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="card flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6">
            <div class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-accent-500/15 text-accent-400 text-lg font-bold">
              02
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Real-Time Multimodal Co-Creation</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
                Lower latency and tighter model integration will make live collaborative sessions —
                where image, motion, and audio respond in near real time to direction — practical for teams and classrooms.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="card flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6">
            <div class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/15 text-emerald-400 text-lg font-bold">
              03
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Provenance, Attribution & Taste Layers</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
                As volume grows, systems that track origin, style lineage, and human contribution will become
                essential for professional pipelines, licensing, and audience trust. Human taste remains the scarce resource.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="card flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6">
            <div class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-amber-500/15 text-amber-400 text-lg font-bold">
              04
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">Personalized Interactive Experiences</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
                Generative systems will power adaptive narratives, dynamic visual worlds, and music that responds
                to individual context — expanding beyond static content into living creative environments.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Closing note -->
    <section class="section-padding border-t border-slate-800/60 bg-slate-900/20">
      <div class="container-narrow text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-4">
          Creativity remains a human practice
        </h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          The most effective practitioners treat generative and agentic systems as amplifiers of intent,
          not replacements for judgment. The tools change; the need for vision, taste, and accountability does not.
        </p>
        <a href="mailto:sales@desertrich.com?subject=Domain%20Acquisition%20Inquiry%20-%20creativeaiexplorer.com" class="btn-primary">
          Inquire about this domain
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
